  "summary": "An alternator (synchronous AC generator) produces alternating current when its rotor field turns inside the stator winding. In a brushless design a small exciter on the same shaft generates AC that rotating diodes rectify to feed the main rotor poles — no brushes or slip rings. The AVR adjusts the exciter field to hold the output voltage constant.",
